Dialogue: 1,0:00:00.00,0:00:36.00,Badge,,0,0,0,,BUILT-IN EXAMPLE / LOCAL PREVIEW
Dialogue: 1,0:00:00.00,0:00:07.00,Caption,,0,0,0,,Your code changed. Did your documentation keep up?\NTruthDiff connects code changes to the docs they may invalidate.
Dialogue: 1,0:00:07.00,0:00:14.00,Caption,,0,0,0,,Start with the verdict.\NRed means a proven mismatch. Amber means review suggested.
Dialogue: 1,0:00:14.00,0:00:22.50,Caption,,0,0,0,,See why it was flagged.\NThis example identifies a removed API route still referenced by a runbook.
Dialogue: 1,0:00:22.50,0:00:29.00,Caption,,0,0,0,,Related does not automatically mean wrong.\NReview suggestions stay separate from proven contradictions.
Dialogue: 1,0:00:29.00,0:00:36.00,Caption,,0,0,0,,Follow the connections in the impact map.\NInspect which changed files connect to affected documents.
Dialogue: 2,0:00:36.00,0:00:42.00,Title,,0,0,0,,{\pos(800,300)}TruthDiff
Dialogue: 2,0:00:36.00,0:00:42.00,End,,0,0,0,,{\pos(800,415)}Code changes. Documentation checked.
Dialogue: 2,0:00:36.00,0:00:42.00,End,,0,0,0,,{\pos(800,510)\c&H00DADF45&}github.com/carlucci001/truthdiff
Dialogue: 2,0:00:36.00,0:00:42.00,End,,0,0,0,,{\pos(800,595)\fs25}Open source / AGPL v3 / No Command Center required
Dialogue: 2,0:00:36.00,0:00:42.00,End,,0,0,0,,{\pos(800,680)\fs23}Try it. Tell us what it catches -- and what it misses.
